// Vellaunos, chief of the elders. Gives the main quest and closes the demo.
=== start
[quest hostages=summoned] -> commission
[quest hostages=reported] -> after
"Well?"
-> hub

=== commission
~ set commissioned
The hall smells of smoke and wet wool. The elders are all here, arguing, and when you come in they stop. Vellaunos waves them out. He waits until the door hide falls shut.

"You've heard. Cenabum. The Carnutes have killed the Roman traders, and Vercingetorix the Arvernian is calling every people in Gaul to war." He rubs his face. "In the spring the Cadurci meet in assembly and decide. Before then, Rome will hear we're thinking about it. You know what Rome does to hostages when their people break faith."

"Three children. My Ateula. The smith's boy Iccios. Your sister." He looks at you as if he's weighing grain. "Somebody has to find them before the assembly. Find where they are and what it would cost to bring them back. I'd go myself if I were twenty years younger and less of a fool. You're neither old nor, I hope, a fool."
* "Where are they?" -> where
* "Why me?" -> whyme

=== whyme
"Because you'll go whether I send you or not, and I'd rather you went with my ring." He pulls it off his finger: plain iron, worn thin. "Show this to any Cadurci and they'll know you speak for Brigodunon. Don't make me regret it."
~ give elders_ring; silver 25
-> where

=== where
[!item elders_ring] He presses his ring into your hand, iron and worn thin, and a purse of silver. "So the Cadurci know you speak for us."
[!item elders_ring] ~ give elders_ring; silver 25
"That's the trouble. We don't know. When the Romans took them, their officer gave us a tally: a stick, notched, with Roman letters burned in. Proof of the pledge, he said. It's been in the shrine five years. Cintugnatos tells me this morning the shrine's been robbed and the tally is gone."

"Nobody here can read Roman anyway. But somebody somewhere can, and it's the only thread we've got. Go and see the vates. Find the tally. Then find someone who can read it."
~ quest hostages find_tally
* "I'll find it." -> END
* "Tell me about the others." -> hostages

=== hub
* [item hostage_tally, quest hostages=find_tally] "I have the tally." -> tally_back
* [quest hostages=north] "I know where the tally was cut." -> report
* [quest grotto=pardon_asked] "Dubnacos has the tally. He wants to come home." -> pardon
* [quest hostages active] "Tell me about the hostages." -> hostages
* "Goodbye." -> END

=== hostages
"Ateula is mine. Twelve when they took her; she'd be seventeen. Clever. Too clever for her own good, her mother said." He stops for a moment. "Iccios is Cobnertos's boy. Big for his age. He wanted to be a smith like his father. And Epona you know better than I do."

"Rome takes the children of the people it doesn't trust, and raises them Roman, or tries. Some come back speaking Latin and wearing their hair short. Some don't come back."
-> hub

=== tally_back
~ quest hostages read_tally; xp 50
[quest grotto active] ~ quest grotto done done
He takes the stick and turns it over in his big hands as if it might speak. Three notches. Letters burned along the side, small and neat and meaningless.

"Rome's letters." He gives it back. "Sulicena, the headwoman at Vindomagos, west along the river. She trades with everyone. Salt to the sea, wine back. If anyone knows who reads this, she will."
* [latin 45] "Let me look at it again. I know some Latin." -> self_read
* "Vindomagos, then." -> END

=== self_read
~ set tally_read; quest hostages north; known noviodunum; xp 75
You hold the tally to the light. The letters are worn, and Roman soldiers abbreviate everything, but you've seen enough of it. A legion number. A name, Lucius something. And at the end, DEP NOVIOD.

"Noviodunum," you say. "A depot. On the Liger, in Aedui country."
-> report

=== report
~ quest hostages reported; xp 150; ending text/demo_end.txt
"Noviodunum." Vellaunos says it slowly. "Aedui country. The Aedui are Rome's oldest friends in Gaul, and they don't like us much." He goes to the door and looks out at the village: smoke, children, a dog asleep in the mud. "It's a long way. Through the Arverni, who are at war, and the Bituriges, who will be. With winter not yet done."

"Go anyway. Take what you need. And {name}: the assembly is in the spring. Whatever you find, I need to know it before then."
* "I'll be back before the spring." -> END

=== pardon
"Dubnacos." He says the name like something he found in his food. "He killed Senovir's son over a cow, three winters ago. Seven winters' exile, that was the judgment, and Senovir thinks it was too soft."

"And now he steals from the gods' shrine and wants to come home for it." He shakes his head. "Give me a reason."
* [speech 45] "Brigodunon is about to need every man who can hold a sword. He's one. Exile doesn't make him any less ours." -> pardon_yes
* [honor >= 15] "Let him come home on my word. If he breaks the peace, the shame is mine." -> pardon_oath
* [PRE 7] "That tally is the only thread to Ateula. What's a cow against your daughter?" -> pardon_yes
* "You're right. Forget I asked." -> hub

=== pardon_oath
~ set pardon_oath
"On your word." He looks at you a long time. "Then it's your word. I'll hold you to it, and so will Senovir."
-> pardon_yes

=== pardon_yes
~ set pardon_granted; quest grotto pardon_granted; xp 50
[!flag pardon_oath] He's quiet a long time. "Damn you. Yes. You're right, and I hate it."
"Tell him he can come home. Tell him he'll pay Senovir the blood price in cattle, every head of it, and he'll sleep outside the rampart till he has. And tell him if he so much as looks at a cow that isn't his, I'll put him back in that cave myself."
-> hub

=== after
"Still here? Noviodunum isn't getting any closer." But he says it gently.
* "Going." -> END
